  "method": "600dpi Poppler rendering; frame/tick affine calibration; select saturated pixels within RGB Euclidean distance8 of256-sample viridis palette with white alpha blending, alpha0.04..1; saturation channel range>=12; convex hull of selected pixel centers. Excludes grayscale resonance lines/text and red theoretical line/stars by color. Explicit masks exclude the printed upper-left legend rectangle and the blue bare-tune circle and the upper-right resonance-label region; the underlying occluded data cannot be recovered. No density cut or endpoint anchoring.",
  "limitations": "Rasterized published image, not raw numerical particles or a probability contour. Rendered pixel-scale ~0.001 tune, but original embedded2092x560 JPEG implies source pixels ~0.0026 tune per panel. Compression, overlapping annotations and threshold add uncertainty; sparse faint points can be lost. This is an approximate visible-color hull, not an exact particle hull. Convex hull fills concavities and is sensitive to visible outliers; no rescaling or fitting to OPALX data.",
